        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall whether a dhatu like \"कवँ\" exists in the dhatupatha, checking against known roots like \"कवृँ वर्णे\" and \"कुङ् शब्दे\" to see which one matches the meaning शब्दे.\n\nFor the luṅ parasmaipada form, I'm working through the application of सिच् with इट्, checking whether vṛddhi applies under 7.2.7 \"अतो हलादेर्लघोः,\" and whether exceptions like 7.2.5 (roots ending in ह्, म्, य्) or 7.2.1's exclusions for वद्/व्रज्/हल्-antaḥ roots would block it for this root ending in व्.\n\nSince कव् doesn't fall under those exceptions, both अकाविषुः and अकविषुः are grammatically possible, but I'm settling on अकविषुः as the answer.\n\n",
